#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078158 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078613 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffb52c1b-a540-5255-8c13-a37940a0d6ec" :knowledge-point/title "Listing the Terms of a Linear Expression"}] :question/id #uuid "65cb74a2-b55a-58e7-951d-2e0c09662f68" :question/math-academy-id "e-12823" :question/problem "List all terms of the expression $3x + 2y - 4x$." :question/worked-solution "We put an addition symbol $(+)$ between each part and separate using parentheses:\n\n$(3x) + (2y) + (-4x)$\nSo, the expression has three terms: $3x$, $2y$, and $-4x$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078159 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078614 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "da99f266-f47f-5fda-8b91-2161c7e48a94" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Particular Terms of an Expression"}] :question/id #uuid "4370fda3-97e7-5fc5-9459-4176f5922431" :question/math-academy-id "e-12824" :question/problem "What is the fourth term of the expression $2t + 5s - \\dfrac{1}{2}s + 8t$?" :question/worked-solution "We put an addition symbol $(+)$ between each part and separate using parentheses:\n\n$$\n(2t) + (5s) + \\left(-\\dfrac{1}{2} s \\right) + (8t)\n$$\n\nCounting off the terms:\n\n- the first term is $2t$,\n- the second term is $5s$,\n- the third term is $-\\dfrac{1}{2}s$, and\n- the fourth term is $8t$.\n\nIn particular, we are interested in the fourth term. The fourth term is $8t$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078160 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078615 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "48f63068-6837-522f-9268-efe63f9c2649" :knowledge-point/title "Equivalent Expressions"}] :question/id #uuid "b8e3ac42-7ade-5b31-8388-1e1061ad3f33" :question/math-academy-id "e-12825" :question/problem "Write down an expression that is equivalent to $9-\\dfrac{1}{2}x+3y$." :question/worked-solution "The expression\n\n$$\n9-\\dfrac{1}{2}x+3y\n$$\n\nhas three terms: $9$,\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{1}{2}x\n$$\n\nand $3y$.\n\nIt doesn't matter 